# Falco ${PLUGIN_NAME} Plugin

A Falco plugin for monitoring ${PLUGIN_NAME} access logs and detecting security threats in real-time.

## Features

- Real-time log monitoring via file watching
- Security threat detection:
  - SQL Injection
  - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
  - Path Traversal / Local File Inclusion
  - Command Injection
  - Suspicious User-Agent Detection
- URL decoding support (up to 3 levels)
- Customizable Falco rules

## Requirements

- Falco 0.36.0+
- Go 1.22+ (for building from source)
- Linux (for running the plugin)

## Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
# Download the plugin binary
wget https://github.com/${AUTHOR}/${PLUGIN_NAME}/releases/latest/download/lib${PLUGIN_NAME}-plugin-linux-amd64.so

# Copy to Falco plugins directory
sudo cp lib${PLUGIN_NAME}-plugin-linux-amd64.so /usr/share/falco/plugins/lib${PLUGIN_NAME}-plugin.so

# Copy rules
sudo cp rules/${PLUGIN_NAME}_rules.yaml /etc/falco/rules.d/
```

### Configuration

Add to your `falco.yaml`:

```yaml
plugins:
  - name: ${PLUGIN_NAME}
    library_path: /usr/share/falco/plugins/lib${PLUGIN_NAME}-plugin.so
    init_config: |
      {"log_paths": ["${LOG_PATH_DEFAULT}"]}

load_plugins: [${PLUGIN_NAME}]

rules_files:
  - /etc/falco/rules.d/${PLUGIN_NAME}_rules.yaml

stdout_output:
  enabled: true
  rate: 0
  max_burst: 0
```

### Running

```bash
# Run Falco with the plugin (plugin-only mode)
sudo falco -c /etc/falco/falco.yaml --disable-source syscall
```

## Building from Source

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/${AUTHOR}/${PLUGIN_NAME}.git
cd ${PLUGIN_NAME}

# Build (auto-detects OS: .dylib on macOS, .so on Linux)
make build

# Run tests
make test

# Verify the binary
make verify
```

### Build Targets

| Target | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `make build` | Standard build — produces `.dylib` on macOS, `.so` on Linux |
| `make build-release` | Size-optimized release build (strips debug symbols) |
| `make verify` | Verify the built binary exports required symbols |

## Testing

### 3-Layer E2E Test Architecture

| Level | Target | Command | Requirement |
|-------|--------|---------|-------------|
| Level 1 | Pattern Coverage | `make e2e-pattern` | No Falco required |
| Level 2 | Pipeline | `make e2e-pipeline` | No Falco required |
| Level 3 | Falco Integration | `make e2e-ci` | Requires Falco |

### Quick Test

```bash
make test      # Unit tests
make e2e       # Level 1 + Level 2
```

## Falco Configuration

| Environment | Config File | Binary |
|-------------|------------|--------|
| Linux (Production) | `falco.yaml` | `.so` |
| macOS (Development) | `falco-local.yaml` | `.dylib` |
| Docker | `falco-docker.yaml` | `.so` |

## Security Rules

| Rule | Description | Priority |
|------|-------------|----------|
| SQL Injection | Detects SQL injection attempts | WARNING |
| XSS | Detects Cross-Site Scripting attempts | WARNING |
| Path Traversal | Detects path traversal / LFI attempts | WARNING |
| Command Injection | Detects command injection attempts | WARNING |
| Suspicious User-Agent | Detects known scanning tools | NOTICE |

## Plugin Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.client_ip` | string | Client IP address |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.method` | string | HTTP method |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.path` | string | Request path |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.query_string` | string | Query string |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.request_uri` | string | Full request URI |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.status` | uint64 | HTTP status code |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.user_agent` | string | User-Agent header |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.bytes_sent` | uint64 | Response body size |
| `${EVENT_SOURCE}.headers[key]` | string | Request headers |

